{
  "requirement": "The Rust caller receives the node's complete `D::NodeContent` or the domain's read error.\n\nThe tool reads a known node, such as the current node or a target from `outgoing_edges`.\nEach page’s `text` contains the next portion of the node’s formatted contents. Formatting follows\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately cover every obligation in `read_node.behavior`. The only citation, `judge.rendering`, is context, so I did not reassess its tests. I did not request any implementation source.\n\n**1. The Rust caller receives the complete `D::NodeContent`.**\n- `direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots` in `tests/validation.rs` reads an empty node and a node of about 16k multi-byte characters (`é` and `終`). The content is larger than a page.\n- It asserts that `read(&1)` and `read_snapshot(&1)` both return content whose `format()` equals the original.\n- It also asserts that the returned values keep the original content after the underlying graph changes.\n- `snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions` checks that `read` returns the current `before` and `after` values.\n\n**2. The Rust caller receives the domain's read error.**\n- In `direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots`, `failed.read(&9).unwrap_err()` equals `\"missing\"`, and no dependency is recorded.\n- `snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions` asserts that `read(&2)` is an error.\n\n**3. The tool reads a known node, either the current node or a target from `outgoing_edges`.**\n- `graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery` calls `outgoing_edges` from node 1, then calls `read_node` on node 2, which is a target of that edge. It asserts the recorded dependencies.\n- `a_complete_node_read_has_text_and_no_continuation` and `graph_read_pages_retain_the_prepared_snapshot_after_contents_change` call `read_node` on node 1, the current node.\n\n**4. Each page's `text` contains the next portion of the formatted contents.**\n- `graph_read_pages_retain_the_prepared_snapshot_after_contents_change` reads multi-byte content that spans two pages.\n- It asserts that the first page has `next` and the second does not.\n- It asserts that the concatenated page `text` values equal the original formatted contents exactly. That rules out gaps, overlaps and split characters.\n- It also holds the snapshot steady while the underlying contents change.\n- `a_complete_node_read_has_text_and_no_continuation` asserts that a short node returns exactly `{\"text\":\"short text\"}`.\n- `concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads` uses a `distinct_pages` formatter and checks that two concurrent agents each get their own pages.\n\n**5. Tool-side failure.**\n- `node_preparation_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents` makes the formatter fail. It asserts that the agent gets an error tool result named `read_node` with the failure text, that the agent continues and submits, and that no dependency is recorded.\n\nI found no plausible requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "ee2df3cbc385f3ca5182bb2e23d957088ef688eaf30a94ffa0611143a4549da9",
